#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-quote.md:6
msgid "The `syn` and `quote` Crates"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-quote.md:8
msgid ""
"Working directly with `TokenStream`s is low-level and tedious. To write "
"procedural macros effectively, authors often rely on **`syn`** (a parser for "
"Rust syntax) and **`quote`** (which constructs `syn` values from literal "
"code fragments) to do the heavy lifting of parsing and code generation."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-quote.md:13
msgid "The workflow of a typical procedural macro is:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-quote.md:15
msgid "**Input:** Accept a raw `proc_macro::TokenStream` from the compiler."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-quote.md:16
msgid ""
"**Parsing (`syn`):** Convert the token stream into a structured, type-safe "
"Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) representing Rust language items (e.g., structs, "
"fields, functions)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-quote.md:19
msgid ""
"**Processing:** Inspect the AST struct and perform your custom logic to "
"decide what code needs to be generated."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-quote.md:21
msgid ""
"**Generation (`quote`):** Use a templated macro to generate a new "
"`proc_macro2::TokenStream`."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-quote.md:23
msgid ""
"**Output:** Convert it back to `proc_macro::TokenStream` and return it to "
"the compiler."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-quote.md:26
msgid "We will look at how `syn` parses code and how `quote` generates code."
msgstr ""
